  "text": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "jane.irwin@stryker.com",
    "text": "<p><a href=\"http://www.stryker.com/en-us/corporate/AboutUs/Newsroom/ProductBulletins/ssLINK/170114\" target=\"_blank\">Results from the DAWN Trial</a> were presented today at the European Stroke Organisation Conference (ESOC), providing compelling evidence that more patients suffering ischemic stroke may benefit from endovascular treatment. While previous randomized clinical trials have proven the benefit of stent retrievers within six hours of stroke onset, the DAWN Trial is the first to evaluate the late-window and wake-up stroke patient population.<br>\n</p>\n<p><b>Read the full article:</b></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.stryker.com/stellent/groups/corporate/documents/web_prod/170114.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Stryker.com</a></p>\n",
